      "writtenOn": "2024-02-22T22:29:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "UCSI specifies an additional 5 bytes of data that Realtek hasn\u0027t implemented.  So we need to open a bug to get Realtek to fix this.\n\nBut we probably want to transition to defining a packed struct matching the UCSI spec.\n\n```\nstruct connector_reset {\n    uint8_t connector_number : 7;\n    enum reset_type reset_type : 1;\n}\n```\n\nThen each driver doesn\u0027t need to pack the data.  It becomes the responsibility of the subsystem to deal with the data.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1533,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1533,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "6c761ab807620cdff7a6a0fb678a3361f1c547de",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1fb2a2ee_8002f5b4",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1533,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-26T18:32:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes there are a number of commands which the UCSI spec has with 6 bytes of data following the `data_len` field. However, the realtek programming guide appears to always truncate the message_len field (2nd byte of the command) to include only up until the last byte which includes at least 1 bit of non-reserved information.",
      "parentUuid": "db3cc7b0_95393a61",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1533,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1533,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "6c761ab807620cdff7a6a0fb678a3361f1c547de",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c7dde7b7_05146de2",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1903,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-22T22:29:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another mismatch between Realtek and UCSI. UCSI specifies 38 bits of reserved at the end, Realtek only specifies 6.\n\nBut I think you should update `union uor_t` to match the UCSI spec.\n\n```\nunion uor_t {\n\tstruct {\n\t\tuint16_t connector_number : 7;\n\t\tuint16_t swap_to_dfp : 1;\n\t\tuint16_t swap_to_ufp : 1;\n\t\tuint16_t accept_dr_swap : 1;\n\t\t/* Reserved */\n\t\tuint16_t reserved_1 : 6;\n\t\tuint32_t reserved_2;\n\t};\n\tuint8_t raw_value[6];\n\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1903,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1903,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "6c761ab807620cdff7a6a0fb678a3361f1c547de",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09aebd3c_0719ebf7",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c",
